          "body": "## Summary\n\nThe conversational Flow guide explains session identity and persistence, but never shows a\ncomplete runnable example, so \"reuse the instance\" and \"resume persisted history\" look the\nsame on paper. This adds one deterministic SQLite-backed example that runs without provider\ncredentials and proves the difference on a fresh instance.\n\nFixes #8070.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `docs/edge/en/guides/flows/conversational-flows.mdx`: a new \"Persisting and resuming a session\" section with the full script, the command, and its expected output. It uses `SQLiteFlowPersistence(\"./notes.db\")` with a stable session id, shows a fresh instance restoring the first turn and appending the second, shows a different session id starting a separate conversation, and states that a restart restores persisted conversation state only — not running background work, in-flight method executions, or open resources. It also says when to call `finalize_session_traces()` if deferral is on.\n- `docs/edge/{ar,ko,pt-BR}/guides/flows/conversational-flows.mdx`: the same section in each locale.\n- `lib/crewai/tests/test_flow_conversation.py`: `TestDocumentedPersistenceExample` runs the documented flow against a temporary SQLite database and asserts the restored history for both the resumed session and the separate one.\n\nThe example uses only existing APIs (`ConversationConfig`, `handle_turn()`, `@persist`, `SQLiteFlowPersistence`) and a deterministic `route_turn`/`@listen` pair, so no LLM is involved.\n\n## Testing\n\nThe documented script prints exactly what the guide claims:\n\n```text\nfirst: [('user', 'buy milk'), ('assistant', 'noted: buy milk')]\nsecond: [('user', 'buy milk'), ('assistant', 'noted: buy milk'), ('user', 'and eggs'), ('assistant', 'noted: and eggs')]\nother: [('user', 'different'), ('assistant', 'noted: different')]\n```\n\n```\npython -m pytest lib/crewai/tests/test_flow_conversation.py -k \"DocumentedPersistenceExample\"\n1 passed, 174 deselected in 24.51s\n```\n\nPython 3.13.14 on Windows. No credentials, no network calls.\n\n## AI assistance\n\nWritten with AI assistance (WorkBuddy) and reviewed before submission.\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Low Risk**\n> Documentation and regression test only; no runtime or API changes.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Adds a **“Persisting and resuming a session”** section to the conversational Flow guides (English, Arabic, Korean, and pt-BR) with a deterministic `NoteTaker` example using `@persist`, `SQLiteFlowPersistence`, and `handle_turn(..., session_id=...)`.\n> \n> The docs contrast **resuming on a fresh instance** with reusing the same in-memory Flow, show expected message history output, and note that restarts restore persisted conversation state only—not in-flight work or open streams—and when to call `finalize_session_traces()` with deferred tracing.\n> \n> **`TestDocumentedPersistenceExample`** in `test_flow_conversation.py` runs the same flow against a temp SQLite DB and asserts resumed vs separate session behavior, locking the guide to existing APIs without an LLM.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 15cbbbfd504c6a88cb6c3765b3bba9eb46bf2f28. Bugbot is set up for automated code reviews on this repo. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->",
